@startuml
title L0 system context: people, application and model services
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
top to bottom direction
actor "Drink learner\nEnglish or Persian" as learner
actor "Local operator\npolicy and evaluation owner" as operator
rectangle "Application boundary / local teaching project" #E8F0FA {
  component "Agentic Drink Book\nReact web interface or Python terminal\ndrinks questions, reviewed replies and session reset" as application #EDF7ED
}
node "Ollama\nexplicit loopback endpoint" as local #FBE9E4
cloud "OpenAI API\nexplicit cloud selection" as cloud #FBE9E4
rectangle "Public deployment requirements / not implemented here" #FFF0D9 {
  component "Verified user identity, TLS and shared limits\nhost isolation, restricted egress and protected audit storage\nincident response and policy ownership" as external
}
learner --> application : ASK / READ
operator --> application : CONFIGURE
application --> local : LOCAL MODE
application --> cloud : CLOUD MODE
external ..> application : BEFORE EXPOSURE
note left of application
Scope: cocktails, ingredients, serving, storage,
fermentation, brewing, wine and spirits production.
Unrelated requests must be refused by policy.
English / Persian presentation; Persian interface is RTL.
end note
note right of application
Four runtime LLM roles; three calls per accepted turn.
A fifth role audits synthetic evaluations when enabled.
Code owns permissions, routing, memory and release.
Incorrect recipes and accepted-refusal retention are known failures.
end note
legend bottom
Solid arrows: supported interactions. Dashed arrow: deployment requirement.
Exactly one provider mode is selected; no automatic cloud fallback.
Cookies identify local browser sessions, not verified people.
Model observations and audit findings can be wrong; no immunity claim.
L0 is this repository's system-context view. Internal components are in L1 (14).
endlegend
footer Agentic Drink Book | Policy 2.1.0 | Model judgments remain fallible
@enduml
